A||||9||Dan010||Opinion about ball joints||||1||
Z||000000||Dan010||11-30-2001||09:07 PM||||Took my 86gt auto to two different shops to have it check.<BR>First one came back and told me that it needed drivers side lower ball joint and inner tie rod end. Was not confident, so I took it to the second shop, told them I add a noise coming from the front only.<BR> They checked it out, and first came back with nothing wrong, then metioned about the other shops findings, they rechecked, this time using the stand to take apply load to lower control arm, came back with both lower ball joints have some movement, and suggested replacing both lower joints.<BR> Now I dont really trust either of these findings. I do not have steering problems, but do have a low knock when I hit bumps in the road. hear it only when the window is down. Also know there is a small amount of movement.<BR>So, should I get it fixed now, or wait till it wears to a greater degree.<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||11-30-2001||09:46 PM||||You are asking a question that should not be answered. Impossible to tell you when/if the ball joint will let go.  It is load separating ball joint, so the weight is constantly pulling it apart.  Sounds like the did check it correctly (eventually) and have told you they are loose.  Take it to the GM dealer if still no sure.<P>Hope this helps.<P><p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-01-2001||12:52 AM||||if one is even questionable, replace all 6 and be done with it. you can replace them yourself with minor effort. <P>The upper front just bolts in. Use a Moog problem solver. it's more adjustable.<P>Pep Boys and Autozone both have loaner tool programs. check with them for the press for the lowers in front and rear.<P>then have it aligned.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eriamjh||12-01-2001||08:53 AM||||You didn't say how many miles were on your '86GT.<P>If you have over 140K, replace them all.  They ARE bad and ready for replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||12-01-2001||11:51 AM||||Hey Dan!<BR>I was waiting to replace my front ball joints, but when the right front seperated, the wait ended...<BR>When you look at the side of your car, does the front look lower than the rear?<BR>Mine looked to be about 2 or 3 inches lower at the time of the seperation, but now the front and rear are at the same height...<BR>The only difference is the new ball joints in front...<P><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan010||12-01-2001||12:54 PM||||Thanks all.<P>Really knew the correct thing to do, just did not want to believe I had to at this time.<BR>But you all are correct!!!!<P>Thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan010||12-02-2001||07:10 PM||||update<BR>Replaced lower ball joints today. Went well, rented the press tool from autozone. Job done but not complete, ball joints were bad, yes, but turns out not to be the only problem, could be time for inner tie-rod, while turning the steering wheel back and forth, still get a knock, seems to be at that joint.<BR> Job for next weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||12-02-2001||07:12 PM||||Huh... Want my opinion on BALL JOINTS? <P>Can't STAND them... Always wearing out 'n stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||87fastback||12-02-2001||07:59 PM||||Dan,  Yes you are correct about needing inner tie rods.  I just went through the same thing on my 87.  Replaced the rack with a used one and it fixed ti a little, then replaced the ball joints with new, but there was still the noise.  New tie rods fixed it all together.  Make sure to get it aligned after!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dan010||12-02-2001||08:51 PM||||Thanks, this is a great place!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
